    "detailed_description": "<strong>Before balls, there were spells!</strong> Challenge your friends individually or by teams in the most crazy and funny sport that has ever existed! Invented in a tavern by a drunken group of adventurers, FireBowl is easy to play and even easier to master (did we already mention that they were all drunk?): hit the fireball, hit other players, kick them when they are on the ground or simply dance... But whatever you do, don't let your sphere get destroyed! It contains a spell that will keep you captive until the wizard acting as referee sobers up.<br><br>You can play alone, but we strongly suggest playing multiplayer modes (as long as you don't mind losing your friends).<br><br>FireBowl will include:<br><br>Arcade Mode - 1 Player<br>Arena Mode - 4 Players VS<br>Singles Match - 2 Players, 1 VS 1<br>Doubles Match - 4 Players, 2 VS 2<br>Dragon's Defy - 1 - 4 Players, Cooperative",
    "about_the_game": "<strong>Before balls, there were spells!</strong> Challenge your friends individually or by teams in the most crazy and funny sport that has ever existed! Invented in a tavern by a drunken group of adventurers, FireBowl is easy to play and even easier to master (did we already mention that they were all drunk?): hit the fireball, hit other players, kick them when they are on the ground or simply dance... But whatever you do, don't let your sphere get destroyed! It contains a spell that will keep you captive until the wizard acting as referee sobers up.<br><br>You can play alone, but we strongly suggest playing multiplayer modes (as long as you don't mind losing your friends).<br><br>FireBowl will include:<br><br>Arcade Mode - 1 Player<br>Arena Mode - 4 Players VS<br>Singles Match - 2 Players, 1 VS 1<br>Doubles Match - 4 Players, 2 VS 2<br>Dragon's Defy - 1 - 4 Players, Cooperative",
    "short_description": "FireBowl is an Arcade Multiplayer game inspired by the classics. It is set in High Fantasy world with all the classic characters such as Halflings, Wizards or... Toilets? Join the party and discover the number one sport of the Middle Ages.",
